# Targets chezmoi DELETES from $HOME on apply. Use sparingly — these are real
# removals, not just "stop managing".
#
# asdf leftovers. asdf was replaced by mise: the binary is gone and ~/.asdf is a
# dead checkout, but these two files were still being read.
#
# .tool-versions is the one that actually broke things. mise reads it in
# addition to ~/.config/mise/config.toml, so a stale
# `java jetbrains-jre-21.0.8b1097.42` line in it made `mise install` fail with
# "no metadata found for version", which aborted the entire `chezmoi apply`.
# Its node and ruby pins now live in ~/.config/mise/config.toml instead.
.tool-versions

# .asdfrc only sets `legacy_version_file = yes`, an asdf-only setting that
# nothing reads any more.
.asdfrc
